  {
    "id": "cli-help",
    "origin": "G10 current",
    "files": {
      ".json": {
        "raw_path": ".private/cli-help.json",
        "sha256": "c2670d771cfed81afc047a7b0eac1c40bea580f24d8d1959ccf83129f51a258a",
        "bytes": 231,
        "text_sanitized": "{\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"orbctl\",\n    \"--help\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \"$WORKSPACES/westlake-harness-g10-env\",\n  \"start\": 1792571966.623731,\n  \"end\": 1792571966.632183,\n  \"rc\": 0,\n  \"timeout_seconds\": 15,\n  \"timed_out\": false\n}\n"
      },
      ".stdout": {
        "raw_path": ".private/cli-help.stdout",
        "sha256": "f332eeb942b5efc74aba21ce8f4910510562afcb89604c0b7068bf076ffc7750",
        "bytes": 1860,
        "text_sanitized": "Use and manage OrbStack and its machines.\n\nThe listed commands can be used with either \"orbctl\" or \"orb\".\n\nYou can also prefix commands with \"orb\" to run them on Linux. For example:\n    orb uname -a\nwill run \"uname -a\" on macOS, and is equivalent to:\n    orbctl run uname -a\n\nIn this mode, the default user and machine will be used.\n\nUsage:\n  orbctl [command]\n\nLinux machines:\n  clone       Clone a machine\n  create      Create a new machine\n  default     Get or set the default machine\n  delete      Delete a machine\n  export      Export a machine to a file\n  import      Import a machine from a file\n  info        Get info about a machine\n  list        List machines\n  logs        Show logs for a machine\n  pull        Copy files from Linux\n  push        Copy files to Linux\n  rename      Rename a machine\n  restart     Restart a machine\n  run         Run command on Linux\n  ssh         Show SSH details\n\nContainers:\n  debug       Debug a Docker container with extra tools\n  docker      Extension commands for Docker\n  k8s         Show commands for using Kubernetes\n\nGeneral:\n  config      Change OrbStack settings\n  doctor      Check if OrbStack is properly configured and in control\n  login       Log in and activate your OrbStack license\n  logout      Log out of your OrbStack account\n  report      Gather info for a bug report\n  reset       Delete all Linux and Docker data\n  serial      Manage serial devices\n  start       Start OrbStack or a machine\n  status      Check whether OrbStack is running\n  stop        Stop OrbStack or a machine\n  top         Show a live activity monitor\n  update      Update OrbStack\n  usb         Manage USB passthrough\n\nAdditional Commands:\n  help        Help about any command\n  version     Show OrbStack version\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for orbctl\n\nUse \"orbctl [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n"
      },
      ".stderr": {
        "raw_path": ".private/cli-help.stderr",
        "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",
        "bytes": 0,
        "text_sanitized": ""
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "status-help",
    "origin": "G10 current",
    "files": {
      ".json": {
        "raw_path": ".private/status-help.json",
        "sha256": "023cc43602623f3fa9ead9f0b92dc131657acc2b9e8ed04eacc56b736df589c5",
        "bytes": 246,
        "text_sanitized": "{\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"orbctl\",\n    \"status\",\n    \"--help\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \"$WORKSPACES/westlake-harness-g10-env\",\n  \"start\": 1792571966.632565,\n  \"end\": 1792571966.6398778,\n  \"rc\": 0,\n  \"timeout_seconds\": 15,\n  \"timed_out\": false\n}\n"
      },
      ".stdout": {
        "raw_path": ".private/status-help.stdout",
        "sha256": "611d289ae57cacb2444a36f5d4ff1e759835c0945133178b012035f0eb5f04d4",
        "bytes": 249,
        "text_sanitized": "Check whether OrbStack is running.\n\nReturns one of the following statuses and exit codes:\n  Running: status 0\n  Starting: status 2\n  Stopped: status 1\n\nUsage:\n  orbctl status [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  orbctl status\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for status\n"
      },
      ".stderr": {
        "raw_path": ".private/status-help.stderr",
        "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",
        "bytes": 0,
        "text_sanitized": ""
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "run-help",
    "origin": "G10 current",
    "files": {
      ".json": {
        "raw_path": ".private/run-help.json",
        "sha256": "d79009d4138aac5c6da6c2d47e817efe2c19f0f2ec8fdb7a8f44daf948be3741",
        "bytes": 243,
        "text_sanitized": "{\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"orbctl\",\n    \"run\",\n    \"--help\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \"$WORKSPACES/westlake-harness-g10-env\",\n  \"start\": 1792571966.640266,\n  \"end\": 1792571966.6482189,\n  \"rc\": 0,\n  \"timeout_seconds\": 15,\n  \"timed_out\": false\n}\n"
      },
      ".stdout": {
        "raw_path": ".private/run-help.stdout",
        "sha256": "c9c1340f24288df3d90c8bc835c59e70ab637de6c8e18dc0348670553d1749a1",
        "bytes": 1123,
        "text_sanitized": "Run a command on Linux.\n\nIf no arguments are provided, an interactive shell is started.\nThe default machine and/or user are used if not specified.\n\nYou can also prefix commands with \"orb\" to run them on Linux. For example:\n    orb uname -a\nwill run \"uname -a\" on Linux, and is equivalent to: orbctl run uname -a\n\nIf you prefer SSH, use \"orb ssh\" for details.\n\nTo run a command on macOS from Linux, use \"macctl run\" instead.\n\nTo pass environment variables, set ORBENV to a colon-separated list of variables:\n\tORBENV=EDITOR:VISUAL orb git commit\n\nPaths are translated automatically when safe.\nTo be explicit, prefix Linux paths with /mnt/linux and macOS paths with /mnt/mac.\n\nUsage:\n  orbctl run [flags] [COMMAND] [ARGS]...\n\nAliases:\n  run, exec, shell\n\nExamples:\n  orbctl run ls\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for run\n  -m, --machine string   Use a specific machine\n  -p, --path             Translate absolute macOS paths to Linux paths\n  -s, --shell            Use the login shell instead of running command directly\n  -u, --user string      Run as a specific user\n  -w, --workdir string   Set the working directory\n"
      },
      ".stderr": {
        "raw_path": ".private/run-help.stderr",
        "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",
        "bytes": 0,
        "text_sanitized": ""
      }
    }
  },
  {
